WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.780 --> 00:00:04.740
Chris Pratt as Booster Gold: It's&nbsp;
a dream casting for some — and a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.740 --> 00:00:08.580
straight-up nightmare for others. Here's the&nbsp;
low-down on the latest split in the DC fandom.

00:00:08.580 --> 00:00:12.660
James Gunn has finally revealed new details&nbsp;
about his and Peter Safran's plans for the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.660 --> 00:00:17.940
future of DC Studios. The first chapter of&nbsp;
Safran and Gunn's rebooted era of the DCU will&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.940 --> 00:00:22.620
be known as "Gods &amp; Monsters." It will feature&nbsp;
a Gunn-penned Superman movie titled Superman:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.620 --> 00:00:26.520
Legacy, a Viola Davis-led Suicide&nbsp;
Squad spin-off show titled Waller,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.520 --> 00:00:30.840
a Green Lantern TV series called Lanterns,&nbsp;
and several other TV and film projects.

00:00:30.840 --> 00:00:35.580
Gunn's long-awaited DC announcement predictably&nbsp;
caused a major stir among comic book fans,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.580 --> 00:00:40.140
and it's not hard to see why. Not only do these&nbsp;
details finally offer some insight into the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.140 --> 00:00:44.700
future of the DCU, but they also include the&nbsp;
debuts of both new and obscure DC comic book&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.700 --> 00:00:49.140
characters. Indeed, one of the more noteworthy&nbsp;
projects announced by Gunn is Booster Gold,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.140 --> 00:00:54.180
a new HBO Max original series that will focus on&nbsp;
a live-action version of its eponymous superhero.

00:00:54.180 --> 00:00:58.583
Very few details have been revealed about&nbsp;
the series, although Gunn did say this:

00:00:58.583 --> 00:01:03.780
"It is basically the superhero story of&nbsp;
imposter syndrome on an HBO Max series."

00:01:03.780 --> 00:01:09.180
Despite how little is actually known about Booster&nbsp;
Gold right now, DC fans are already engaging in an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.180 --> 00:01:13.380
intense debate online about whether or not one&nbsp;
major movie star should play the titular hero.

00:01:13.380 --> 00:01:17.940
Earlier this month, some DC fans began calling&nbsp;
for Guardians of the Galaxy star Chris Pratt&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.940 --> 00:01:21.540
to be cast as a live-action version of&nbsp;
Booster Gold. Over a week before James&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.540 --> 00:01:25.580
Gunn announced the comic book character's&nbsp;
HBO Max series, one Twitter user said:

00:01:28.171 --> 00:01:32.580
In the immediate hours after Gunn's DC slate&nbsp;
announcement, several fans began to reiterate&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:32.580 --> 00:01:36.840
their desire to see Pratt play Booster Gold&nbsp;
in the DCU, too. On Twitter, one person wrote:

00:01:44.468 --> 00:01:45.268
Another said:

00:01:49.007 --> 00:01:52.440
Of course, not every DC fan thinks&nbsp;
Pratt is the right actor to play the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.440 --> 00:01:55.980
character. Following Gunn's recent&nbsp;
DC announcement, one person tweeted:

00:02:00.660 --> 00:02:01.380
Another said:

00:02:05.064 --> 00:02:09.420
All in all, it seems safe to say that DC fans&nbsp;
aren't in total agreement right now about whether&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.420 --> 00:02:13.860
Pratt should actually be cast as Booster Gold.&nbsp;
Then again, it's worth noting that James Gunn&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.860 --> 00:02:17.700
hasn't suggested that he's even considering&nbsp;
Pratt for the role. The filmmaker has said&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.700 --> 00:02:21.480
that he'll likely end up working with members of&nbsp;
his Guardians of the Galaxy cast again, however,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.480 --> 00:02:25.920
so there's definitely a chance Pratt could show&nbsp;
up at some point in the Gunn-led era of the DCU.

00:02:25.920 --> 00:02:29.880
Nevertheless, Pratt is far from the only&nbsp;
actor who could be chosen to take on the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:29.880 --> 00:02:34.140
lead role in Booster Gold. As a matter of&nbsp;
fact, some DC fans have already begun to list&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.140 --> 00:02:37.800
other actors who they believe would be right&nbsp;
for the beloved DC Comics role. On Twitter,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:37.800 --> 00:02:42.420
one DC fan called for Gunn and Peter Safran to&nbsp;
cast Top Gun: Maverick breakout Glen Powell as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.420 --> 00:02:46.620
the DCU's Booster Gold. One user named&nbsp;
Stranger Things star Joe Keery as their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.620 --> 00:02:50.820
top choice to play the DC superhero, while&nbsp;
another suggested Jensen Ackles for the role.

00:02:50.820 --> 00:02:55.200
Clearly, Booster Gold's casting is up in the air&nbsp;
right now. One thing that is for sure, however,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.200 --> 00:02:58.800
is that he'll likely be a superhero&nbsp;
unlike any other: In the comics,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:58.800 --> 00:03:03.180
Booster Gold is a man from the 25th century&nbsp;
who uses the era's technology to travel back&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:03.180 --> 00:03:07.080
in time and become a superhero of the&nbsp;
past. He certainly isn't like many of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.080 --> 00:03:10.620
the other comic book characters that Gunn and&nbsp;
Safran plan to focus on in the coming years.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:10.620 --> 00:03:14.820
Whoever plays him will be given the chance to&nbsp;
not only get in on the ground floor of Gunn&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:14.820 --> 00:03:19.440
and Safran's new DCU, but also portray one&nbsp;
of the franchise's most intriguing heroes.

